-- title:
--   pp.11–12 — $\mathbb E(\theta_{k,t+1}\mid\mathcal F_t)=\theta_{k,t}(1-N_t^{-\alpha}+(N_t+1)^{-\alpha})\le\theta_{k,t}$
-- statement:
--   For each $k\in[K]$ and $t\ge0$,
--   $$\mathbb E(\theta_{k,t+1}\mid\mathcal F_t)=\theta_{k,t}\Big(1-\frac1{N_t^\alpha}+\frac1{(N_t+1)^\alpha}\Big)\le\theta_{k,t}.$$
--
--   The identity gives the supermartingale property of the voting power, and shows how much of it is lost per period.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the Poly(α) rule described by (2.3)–(2.6), K ∈ ℕ₊ bidders, stakes n_{k,t} → `Model μ K α n₀`: the joint conditional one-step law, stakes in Fin K → ℕ, real α ≥ 0 with Real.rpow, and 1 ≤ N; reason: the conditional one-step law and n₀ determine the law of the chain; 1 ≤ N only keeps N_t^{−α} defined
--   - generalization: F_t generated by the events S_{k,r}, r ≤ t → any filtration ℱ to which n is adapted and for which the one-step law holds; reason: the natural filtration of n is one such ℱ, so the statement specializes to the paper's F_t
-- source:
--   Tang & Yao, Polynomial Voting Rules, arXiv:2206.10105v5, proof of Theorem 6 (ii), pp.11–12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PolyVoting_Model

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace PolyVoting

/-- **The one-step identity for the voting power** (Tang & Yao, *Polynomial Voting Rules*,
arXiv:2206.10105v5, pp.11–12): `E(θ_{k,t+1} | F_t) = θ_{k,t} (1 - 1 / N_t ^ α + 1 / (N_t + 1) ^ α)`,
and the right side is at most `θ_{k,t}`. -/
theorem power_condExp {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {μ : Measure Ω}
    [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] {K : ℕ} {α : ℝ} {n₀ : Fin K → ℕ} (M : Model μ K α n₀)
    (k : Fin K) (t : ℕ) :
    (μ[M.power k (t + 1) | M.ℱ t] =ᵐ[μ] fun ω =>
      M.power k t ω *
        (1 - 1 / (M.total t ω : ℝ) ^ α + 1 / ((M.total t ω : ℝ) + 1) ^ α)) ∧
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, M.power k t ω *
        (1 - 1 / (M.total t ω : ℝ) ^ α + 1 / ((M.total t ω : ℝ) + 1) ^ α) ≤ M.power k t ω := by sorry

end PolyVoting
